job_description:
About Kepler
Kepler executes engineered marketing, where every message and ad delivered helps create a more personalized and productive relationship between brands and their consumers. We do this by acting as clients’ agency of record, as their in-house team, or some hybrid of the two – and by harnessing data and technology across all paid digital media and data-driven CRM channels.
• We're transparent with our employees. You'll hear updates on company financials, how we're performing against bonus goals, and how we're responding to challenges we face.&nbsp;
• We're growing. For you, that means unparalleled growth opportunities and a role in shaping the direction of the company.&nbsp;
• We're fun. You'll work with and learn from the smartest people in the industry and have a blast doing it.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Overview
The Strategy &amp; Activation team is the main interface between our clients and the rest of the business. We are not only responsible for building great relationships with our clients and delivering award winning digital campaigns, we are also accountable for the growth and development of our client’s businesses. Whether that involves being first to market with new digital channels, supporting measurement journeys, providing innovative optimisation solutions or educational workshops, we pride ourselves on the strong client partnerships built.&nbsp;
We are currently looking for a&nbsp;Manager to join the team and become part of our close-knit family of passionate Activators.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Role Overview
The Manager plays a key role within the Strategy &amp; Activation team. Reporting into the Associate Director or Senior Manager, the Manager owns all client operational work from media responses and planning to campaign set-up and optimisation within the digital buying platforms. You will work closely with Analysts to ensure campaigns run smoothly and deliver to the campaign goals.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
About the Role
• Lead day to day contact with clients (calls and/or face-to-face) to ensure campaign planning and management is in-line with client expectations, providing feedback and data driven recommendations on how to achieve the best performance
• Build strong client relationships, anticipating needs that support their primary focus areas
• Create cross-channel digital brief responses and media plans which effectively meet client business and campaign goals, providing a clear rationale
• Collaborate with external media and creative agencies to ensure cohesive planning and optimal campaign execution&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Manage campaign execution &amp; QA within the buying platforms, proactively troubleshooting issues as they arise
• Optimise campaign performance (brand and/or acquisition) against forecasts, driving results for continued improvement and providing new ideas and solutions&nbsp;
• Provide clear and concise insight and analysis of campaign results across the various digital channels and devices (Display, Video, Social, Search, Audio, OOH etc)
• Build relationships with key media partners and technology vendors (e.g. Google, Meta, Amazon) to deliver best in class service and opportunities for our clients
• Identify additional revenue opportunities and create accompanying proposals
• Train and coach Analysts to develop and grow within the team&nbsp;
• Work with the other (Senior) Managers to brainstorm and implement wider company and client focused initiatives
&nbsp;
Desired Experience and Skills
• 2+ years of hands-on in platform experience, ideally across a minimum of 2 of the following digital channels: Programmatic Display, Video, Paid Search and/or Paid Social
• Extensive Google Ads in-platform experience is required
• Digital planning experience (client, agency or DSP side)&nbsp;
• A proven passion for digital media/advertising &amp; technology
• Strong people &amp; communication skills
• Excellent client service approach and ability to multitask with great attention to detail
• A technical/analytical mindset
• Enjoyment when working as part of a team
• Coaching or line management experience
&nbsp;
Salary
Our compensation strategy is designed to attract, reward, and retain the talented employees that drive Kepler’s growth and success. We aim to offer competitive direct compensation that demonstrates the value we place on our employees and their well-being.
Our salary banding for this role starts at £41,800 per annum.
&nbsp;
Benefits
• 25 days annual leave, increasing to 28 days after 3 years. Option to buy additional annual leave allowance up to 30 per year
• Healthcare cash plan
• Monthly Wellness Allowance&nbsp;
• Ride to work cycle scheme
• Season ticket loan scheme
• ‘Work from Anywhere’ (WFA) for up to 4 weeks per year
• Hybrid working 3 days onsite and 2 days remote per week
• Flexible working with start and finish times between 8am - 10am and 4.30pm - 6.30pm
• Company pension contributions
• Enhanced parental leave policies
• Annual tuition budgets for out of work study
• Mobile phone, home broadband reimbursements
• Working from home equipment budget
• Weekly free breakfast, fruit and drinks
• Regular paid socials, and social budgets
&nbsp;
The increasing adoption of AI is reshaping our industry. As part of your application, please include a brief disclosure of which AI tools (if any) you have used to assist with your preparation. Our interview process includes a discussion surrounding your experience experimenting with these tools and how to leverage them effectively within a professional setting. Please be aware that in line with GDPR, we do not allow use of AI for recording/transcripts during interviews without all attendees consent.
Please note that, at this time and for this position, we cannot accommodate long term future sponsorship needs for UK work authorisation. Please note in your application if you fall under this category.
Protect yourself from recruitment fraud. The only way to apply for a position at Kepler is by submitting a direct application via the Keplergrp.com&nbsp;website&nbsp;or working with a recruiter employed by Kepler with a @keplergrp.com&nbsp;email address.&nbsp;Learn how to stay safe by clicking&nbsp;here&nbsp;

Keystone is a premier economics, technology, and strategy consulting firm built to help companies lead through transformation. As breakthrough innovations reshape industries, redefine competition and change our society, complex and highly competitive ecosystems emerge. Keystone advises technology leaders, Fortune 100 companies, their legal counsel, and governments on business, economic, litigation, and regulatory strategy in relation to these innovations and competitive eco-systems. We operate globally from offices in Boston, New York City, San Francisco, Seattle, Washington, D.C., London, Dubai, and Bengaluru.
We’re growing quickly and looking for an exceptional Engagement Manager&nbsp;to help clients move from AI ambition to AI-native execution. This role is designed for someone who combines structured consulting judgment with hands-on fluency in agentic AI systems, modern technology architecture, and rigorous analytical problem-solving.&nbsp;
About the&nbsp;Engagement Manager – Data &amp; AI Strategy&nbsp;Role&nbsp;
This role&nbsp;will work at the intersection of strategy, technology, and execution. You will scope ambiguous business problems, develop testable hypotheses, conduct rigorous analysis, and translate findings into clear client-ready recommendations. Just as importantly, you will operate as a builder: using, managing, and improving AI agents as part of the delivery team to accelerate workflows, raise quality, and create tangible client value.&nbsp;
This is not a traditional strategy consulting role with AI as an additional topic. Success requires being AI-native and high comfort working directly with AI tools, managing human-in-the-loop workflows, and partnering with technical and non-technical stakeholders to prototype and operationalize AI-enabled solutions.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Key Responsibilities&nbsp;
Drive AI-Native Strategy Work&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Structure ambiguous client problems into clear workplans, hypotheses, analyses, and recommendations.
• Conduct independent research, market analysis, technology landscape assessments, and competitive benchmarking.
• Synthesize complex findings into crisp narratives for client executives, technical teams, and internal leadership.
• Help identify high-impact AI use cases and translate them into pragmatic execution roadmaps.&nbsp;
Manage AI Agents as Part of the Delivery Team&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Use agentic AI systems to complete and accelerate core consulting workflows, including research, synthesis, analysis, drafting, QA, and knowledge management.
• Manage AI agents for quality, integration, human-in-the-loop review, and optimal contribution to project outcomes.
• Design repeatable AI-enabled workflows that improve speed, rigor, and client value.
• Evaluate outputs critically and maintain high standards for accuracy, judgment, and confidentiality.&nbsp;
Build, Prototype, and Implement&nbsp;
• Work directly with AI tools rather than only advising from a distance.
• Prototype solutions, prompts, workflows, and light technical approaches alongside clients and internal teams.
• Partner with engineers, data scientists, and business stakeholders to understand feasibility, constraints, and implementation paths.
• Bring a practical understanding of cloud infrastructure, data pipelines, LLM integration, and enterprise software ecosystems to client work.&nbsp;
Own Client-Ready Deliverables&nbsp;
• Prepare high-quality analyses, memos, presentations, and executive communications.
• Manage discrete workstreams with strong ownership, judgment, and attention to detail.
• Contribute to client meetings and workshops with clear communication and structured thinking.
• Operate effectively in fast-paced, ambiguous environments where priorities evolve quickly.&nbsp;
What You’ll Bring&nbsp;
Required&nbsp;
• 5+ years' experience in strategy consulting, business strategy, AI strategy, product strategy, technology strategy, or similarly rigorous analytical project work.
• High level of comfort using AI tools and agentic workflows directly in professional work, including tasking agents, reviewing outputs, identifying gaps, and improving workflow quality.
• Ability to evaluate AI-assisted outputs for quality, accuracy, business relevance, and client readiness.
• Proven ability to translate research, expert input, client context, and AI-generated outputs into polished client-facing materials.
• Practical understanding of how business processes can be broken down, documented, and redesigned for AI-enabled delivery.
• Proven builder orientation: willingness to roll up sleeves, use tools directly, prototype workflows, and implement practical solutions with clients.
• Working fluency in modern AI and enterprise technology architecture, including cloud infrastructure, data pipelines, enterprise software, and LLM integration.
• Exceptional structured problem-solving, analytical, and quantitative skills, including rigorous research, market analysis, and technology landscape assessment.
• Excellent communication and presentation skills for both technical and non-technical stakeholders.
• Adaptability, resilience, and ownership in fast-paced client-service environments.&nbsp;
Preferred&nbsp;
• Prior experience at a top-tier consulting firm, AI-native company, technology company, or high-growth product environment.
• Experience supporting AI transformation, workflow automation, knowledge management, or enterprise AI adoption initiatives.
• Familiarity with prompt engineering, AI evaluation, RAG workflows, data governance, or responsible AI practices.
• Experience working directly with senior clients or cross-functional executive stakeholders.
• Exposure to economics, litigation, regulatory, financial services, legal, or other complex analytical domains.&nbsp;
What Sets You Apart&nbsp;
• Exceptional intellectual horsepower and structured judgment.
• Bias toward building, testing, and improving rather than producing theoretical recommendations only.
• High standards for quality, precision, and ownership.
• Ability to move fluidly between strategy, technology, analysis, and client communication.
• Intellectual curiosity about how AI changes business models, workflows, and competitive dynamics.&nbsp;
Why Join Us
• Help build an AI-native advisory capability inside a premier economics, technology, and strategy consulting firm.
• Work on complex, high-stakes client problems where AI can materially change outcomes.
• Operate with exceptional colleagues across technology, economics, management science, and strategy.
• Develop rapidly in a team that values ownership, rigor, and practical innovation.&nbsp;
The salary range below represents total annual compensation. Actual compensation will depend upon the level the individual is hired into based on their experience, knowledge, skills and qualifications. In addition to annual salary, we offer a comprehensive benefits package and a culture grounded in integrity, curiosity, and teamwork.&nbsp;
Annual Pay Range
£147,000&mdash;£197,000 GBP
&nbsp;
At Keystone, we value the varied backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives our colleagues bring to our firm. We are committed to building an inclusive culture where everyone feels respected, has a sense of belonging, and has opportunities to grow.
This commitment extends to how we hire. Keystone is an equal opportunity employer committed to fair and inclusive hiring practices. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.

LHV Bank Limited is a UK-licensed bank operating across three core business segments: Retail Banking, SME Lending, and Banking Services (BaaS). The bank is a wholly owned subsidiary of LHV Group, a listed financial services provider headquartered in Estonia. LHV Bank operates under a full UK banking licence granted in May 2023.
The Bank supports over 200 fintech clients with embedded financial infrastructure, provides retail savings products via digital channels, and offers SME credit solutions across the UK. In line with its regulatory responsibilities and growth ambitions, LHV Bank is committed to maintaining a robust and proportionate financial crime control environment.
Expanding our services, LHV Bank now provides personal banking solutions. Our offerings include current accounts with competitive interest rates, fixed-rate bonds for long-term savings, and debit cards.&nbsp; Customers can conveniently access these services through the LHV App, enabling secure account opening and management.
Role overview&nbsp;
Lead the strategy and delivery of the bank’s customer data, CRM and customer operations platforms, including AI-supported customer service. Improve customer data quality and consistency, and ensure platforms and processes are scalable, well controlled and clearly owned.&nbsp;
Own product direction, the domain roadmap and customer data requirements, working with Engineering, Data and business owners on design and delivery. Lead and develop the Product Manager and Business Analyst, delegating platform prioritisation and continuous improvement to the PM and requirements analysis and delivery support to the BA.&nbsp;
Work closely with Engineering, Data, Compliance, Risk and Customer Operations. Deliver agreed data and platform dependencies for AFC, segment onboarding, Single Customer View (SCV), tax reporting and data retention programmes, while ownership of those areas remains with the relevant teams.&nbsp;
This is a hands-on leadership role in a small bank, combining strategic direction with practical delivery through clear delegation and effective partnerships.&nbsp;
Key accountabilities&nbsp;
• Own and deliver the domain strategy and roadmap, balancing customer needs, business value, regulatory requirements, risk and available capacity.&nbsp;
• Own the customer data model, requirements and quality standards, working with Engineering, Data and business owners to standardise definitions, control changes and prioritise improvements across business lines.&nbsp;
• Establish clear ownership, intake, prioritisation, processes and controls across the domain, managing and escalating risks within agreed authority.&nbsp;
• Embed relevant data protection, financial crime and Consumer Duty requirements into product design and delivery, working with accountable business and control owners.&nbsp;
• Lead the product direction and controlled adoption of AI-supported customer service, agreeing use cases, monitoring, human escalation and fallback arrangements with relevant teams.&nbsp;
• Guide platform investment and lifecycle decisions, assessing whether to extend, buy, build, consolidate or retire solutions based on evidence, cost, risk and long-term value.&nbsp;
• Define and monitor measures of data quality, platform adoption, customer outcomes and operational efficiency, using findings to prioritise improvements and assess supplier performance.&nbsp;
• Build alignment across business lines, technical teams and senior stakeholders, securing agreement on priorities, investment and dependencies, including potential group-wide harmonisation or migration.&nbsp;
• Lead and develop the PM and BA, setting clear expectations, delegating responsibility and coaching them to deliver agreed outcomes.&nbsp;
Experience&nbsp;
Essential&nbsp;
• Experience owning a product area and roadmap, applying discovery, prioritisation and outcome measurement to deliver measurable improvements.&nbsp;
• Experience leading and developing people through effective delegation, coaching and clear accountability.&nbsp;
• Ownership of a CRM or customer operations platform in a regulated environment.&nbsp;
• Strong understanding of customer data models, quality, integrations and change control, with sufficient technical confidence to challenge proposals and assess trade-offs with Engineering and Data.&nbsp;
• Practical experience applying UK financial services and data protection requirements to customer data or customer operations products.&nbsp;
• Experience establishing clear ownership, prioritisation and governance across teams, and influencing senior stakeholders across business, technical and control functions.&nbsp;
• Evidence of balancing strategic priorities with hands-on delivery in a changing environment with competing demands and limited resources.&nbsp;
&nbsp;Desirable&nbsp;
• Salesforce experience.&nbsp;
• Experience with AI-supported customer service or automation.&nbsp;
• Experience of data migration or group-wide harmonisation.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Some of our benefits (only applicable to UK based roles not Internship programmes)&nbsp;
• Competitive salary &amp;lots of opportunities to learn, grow and progress professionally.
• Open and inclusive culture.&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Hybrid working.
• Fantastic offices and great working environment.
• Vitality Health Plan (includes private health insurance, travel insurance, gym discounts)&nbsp;
• Health cash Plan (Medicash health plan Level 3)
• 6% employer pension contribution.
• Life assurance – 4 x salary.
• Income protection insurance – 75%&nbsp;&nbsp;
• 28 days holiday plus 3 additional days, &amp; further days for various key life events as well as the opportunity to sell up to 5 days per calendar year.
• Swap&nbsp;public/bank holidays each year for alternative days that align with your personal, cultural, or religious observances.&nbsp;
• Enhanced family friendly and family forming policies.
• Access to a wide range of retail discounts.&nbsp;
• Team Socials.&nbsp;

Some key info for you about Liberis:&nbsp;
🌱 We were founded in 2007
💰 We have provided over $3bn of funding to small businesses so far
🚀 We have been named in&nbsp;CNBC &amp; Statista Top 150 UK Fintechs for 2025
🌍 We're a global team, with a dynamic presence in&nbsp;6&nbsp;key locations around the world
🧠 We're a thriving community of over&nbsp;290&nbsp;innovative minds
👩🏾 🤝 👨🏼 We're a vibrant melting pot, celebrating over&nbsp;27&nbsp;nationalities in our team
🏢 Our team brings experience from over&nbsp;740&nbsp;previous companies, from startups to global giants
🎯 We have just been named as one of&nbsp;FinTech’s Finest 50&nbsp;by Welcome to the Jungle
💪 We’re proud to be an accredited&nbsp;Real Living Wage&nbsp;employer, ensuring everyone is paid fairly for the great work they do!
&nbsp;
The team
We are the Risk team responsible for managing the credit risk of Liberis’ portfolios, which include designing effective new strategies, managing the credit quality of our products across geographies, and providing specialist credit risk advice to the business.
The Risk team is based in London and covers Risk analytics, Decision Science, Underwriting and Collections. Our mission is to grow Liberis profitably to become the leading embedded business finance provider and we are now looking for a Credit Risk Analyst to join us on this journey.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
The role
&nbsp;
We're looking for someone who enjoys solving complex problems through data and analysis. This is an ideal role for an analytical thinker who is naturally curious, enjoys investigating trends and identifying opportunities, and is motivated by seeing their work influence real business decisions.
You'll be comfortable taking ownership of projects - framing problems, conducting deep analysis, developing recommendations and working with stakeholders to implement change. While experience in credit risk is beneficial, we're primarily looking for an individual with strong analytical capability, commercial thinking and a track record of turning data into actionable insights.
Reporting to the Risk Manager, you'll help shape Liberis' credit risk strategy by delivering analytical insights, developing portfolio monitoring frameworks and driving strategic initiatives across our global products. You'll work closely with teams across Risk, Data Science, Analytics, Product, Pricing and Commercial to ensure our lending decisions support sustainable growth while remaining within our risk appetite.
&nbsp;
What you'll get to do:&nbsp;
• Build and improve portfolio monitoring frameworks, turning data into clear insights and recommendations.
• Monitor losses, delinquencies, inactivity, repayment trends and vintage performance to assess portfolio health and identify emerging risks.
• Investigate changes in performance, explain their causes and identify opportunities to improve outcomes or support growth.
• Use your analysis to inform credit risk strategies, including where customer eligibility could be expanded or tightened.
• Develop forecasting models to better understand future risk and contribute to budgeting and planning.
• Work with colleagues across risk and the first line to understand problems, communicate findings and recommend action.
• Deliver analytical projects across the portfolio, showing how your work contributes to business decisions rather than stopping at a report or dashboard.
&nbsp;
The interview process:
• Screening call with Chess (Internal Recruiter) (30 mins)
• Video interview with the Hiring Manager (1 hour)
• Task based interview with the Risk Team (90 mins)
&nbsp;
What we think you'll need
• Hands-on data analysis skills, including SQL or BigQuery experience, and the ability to apply those skills to unfamiliar tools. Our current analytics environment includes BigQuery and Looker.
• The ability to move from data to an explanation: identifying patterns, investigating why they're happening and making practical recommendations.
• Clear communication, including the ability to explain your own contribution to a project, your analytical approach and what changed as a result.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Next steps&nbsp;If this opportunity feels like the right fit for your next career move, we’d love to hear from you!
Even if you don’t meet every requirement, don’t hesitate to apply or reach out to Chess (Internal Recruiter) on&nbsp;chess.crossley@liberis.com
&nbsp;
Our hybrid approach
Working together in person helps us move faster, collaborate better and build a great Liberis culture. Our hybrid working approach requires colleagues to attend the office at least three days a week, increasing to at least four days a week in Q1 2027
&nbsp;
&nbsp;#LI-FC1&nbsp;
&nbsp;

Some key info for you about Liberis:&nbsp;
🌱 We were founded in 2007
💰 We have provided over $3bn of funding to small businesses so far
🚀 We have been named in&nbsp;CNBC &amp; Statista Top 150 UK Fintechs for 2025
🌍 We're a global team, with a dynamic presence in&nbsp;6&nbsp;key locations around the world
🧠 We're a thriving community of over&nbsp;290&nbsp;innovative minds
👩🏾 🤝 👨🏼 We're a vibrant melting pot, celebrating over&nbsp;27&nbsp;nationalities in our team
🏢 Our team brings experience from over&nbsp;740&nbsp;previous companies, from startups to global giants
🎯 We have just been named as one of&nbsp;FinTech’s Finest 50&nbsp;by Welcome to the Jungle
💪 We’re proud to be an accredited&nbsp;Real Living Wage&nbsp;employer, ensuring everyone is paid fairly for the great work they do!
&nbsp;
Our Product &amp; Engineering Team:
Liberis is building the embedded finance platform that lets partners around the world offer innovative funding products to their small business customers. We're a growth-stage fintech with teams in London, Nottingham, Atlanta, Stockholm, Munich and Mumbai, and we’re building a global Product, Data &amp; Engineering team that thrives on autonomy, ownership, and is focused on impact! Our teams solve real-world problems for small businesses, shaping products that unlock opportunity at scale.&nbsp;
Engineering is going through an AI-first transformation, rethinking how teams are structured and how they ship. It's changing what a small team can do! We empower our teams to make decisions, move fast, and take full responsibility for the solutions they deliver. You’ll join a team where curiosity is encouraged and collaboration across Product, Data, Delivery and Engineering is the norm.
&nbsp;
The role:
Turn new partner opportunities into lending solutions that deliver for Liberis and our partners. As Product Solutions Lead, you’ll work across Business Development, Product, Risk and Technology to shape what we offer, how it works and the commercial case behind it.
Reporting to the Head of Solutions and GTM, you’ll bring a product mindset to partner conversations, balancing ambition, commercial value and technical feasibility. You’ll own the solution scope and commercial outcomes, working closely with the teams responsible for programme delivery and technical implementation.
This is a new role with the autonomy to shape how the solutions function operates. Your work will span products, partners and regions, giving you meaningful influence over the team’s ways of working and future direction.
&nbsp;
What you'll get to do:
• Work with Business Development and prospective partners to understand their needs, assess opportunities in new regions and partner types, and define the right product and commercial approach
• Build business cases using existing financial models to understand revenue potential, costs and the drivers of a successful lending programme
• Turn partner problems into clear requirements, aligning Product, Risk and Technology on what we can deliver and which capabilities we need to develop
• Define a clear scope for delivery teams and stay accountable for the solution's commercial performance as it moves towards launch
• Manage and develop a your team, establishing practical frameworks and processes as the function grows
• Feed partner insights and gaps in our offering into the team's strategy
&nbsp;
The interview process:
• Screening call with Chess (Internal Recruiter) (30 mins)
• Video interview with the Hiring Manager (1 hour)
• Case study interview (90 mins)
• Video interview with the wider Liberis team&nbsp;(1 hour)
&nbsp;
What we think you'll need:
• Product management or closely related experience: you can understand a problem, define requirements and work effectively with technology teams.&nbsp;
• Experience working with enterprise clients or partners, including navigating their stakeholders and decision-making processes.&nbsp;
• Commercial judgement: you can assess a business case, use Excel models and explain what makes an opportunity financially worthwhile.
• Enough technical fluency to read API documentation and contribute to integration discussions. You don't need to code or design the technical implementation.
• The ability to influence without direct authority, handle difficult conversations and bring commercial and technical teams to a shared decision.
• A hands-on approach to ambiguity: you can move work forward while improving the processes around it.
• Experience in lending or embedded finance would be particularly useful. Payments, marketplaces, cards or open banking experience would also help.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Next steps&nbsp;If this opportunity feels like the right fit for your next career move, we’d love to hear from you!
Even if you don’t meet every requirement, don’t hesitate to apply or reach out to Chess (Internal Recruiter) on&nbsp;chess.crossley@liberis.com
&nbsp;
Our hybrid approach
Working together in person helps us move faster, collaborate better and build a great Liberis culture. Our hybrid working approach requires colleagues to attend the office at least three days a week, increasing to at least four days a week in Q1 2027
&nbsp;
&nbsp;#LI-FC1&nbsp;
&nbsp;
