Senior Economist, Tourism Economics
Department: Tourism Economics EMEA
Employment Type: Full Time
Location: London, UK
Description
Tourism Economics is a subsidiary of Oxford Economics dedicated to analytically-based consulting to the tourism sector. Oxford Economics is one of the world’s leading economics consultancies, providing advice to international institutions, governments and blue-chip companies. We are looking to hire a Senior Economist to join the consulting team at Tourism Economics. Our team provides a range of analytical services to clients, including:
• Quantifying the economic impact of tourism-related industries, companies, events, and visitor segments;
• Developing tourism satellite accounts;
• Performing cost-benefit analyses of public policies;
• Examining the return on investment of infrastructure development and marketing expenditures; and • Constructing tailored forecasts for various visitor segments.
This role will be based within the EMEA consulting team. Consulting projects usually run for between two and six months, and culminate in a report or presentation to a client. The Senior Economist role will entail significant contributions to major projects and managing other smaller projects.
Senior Economists collaborate closely with Lead Economists and Associate Directors on all aspects of client engagements. Their responsibilities range from contributing to the design of methodologies and writing proposals to project management, conducting analysis, and communicating results to the client. Project teams generally consist of one or two economists and, when needed, specialised econometric modellers.
A core part of the role will involve implementing quantitative models using a variety of analytical tools such as IO modelling, cost-benefit analysis, or econometric analysis. The post-holder will report to the Associate Director of Consulting, EMEA.
Key Responsibilities
• Managing and overseeing smaller research studies;
• Ensuring robust and rigorous economic analysis in the delivery of consultancy projects;
• Applying and assuring quantitative analytical techniques as applied to large datasets;
• Handling clients and potential clients effectively and developing Tourism Economics’ relationship with them;
• Assisting in the development of research proposals, project reports, and presentations;
• Planning and structuring projects, and coordinating input from a range of team members, ensuring sufficient time for quality assurance; • Being entrepreneurial and proactive in the identification and pursuit of new business opportunities; and
• For the right candidate, line management of one or two team members, to ensure resources are allocated efficiently and to support professional development.
Skills, Knowledge & Expertise
• Extensive experience of client-facing work and the ability to develop commercial relationships with potential clients;
• Substantial experience of economic analysis, including familiarity with analytical techniques such as IO modelling, cost-benefit analysis and econometrics.
• Excellent analytical skills;
• Evidence of being proactive and creative in using economics to answer (external, internal or policymaker) clients’ questions;
• Very strong written and verbal communication, including the ability to explain economic concepts and quantitative results, as well as their implications, to non-specialists; and
• Excellent attention to detail and a commitment to going the extra mile to produce rigorous, accurate work, within the constraints of the time and resources available.
Desirable:
• Experience in managing consulting projects within the tourism sector
• A post-graduate degree in economics;
• Experience with quantitative analysis software such a s Python, R, Stata;
• Experience of client-facing work and the ability to develop commercial relationships with potential clients
Job Benefits
Here are some of the benefits we offer in the UK to ensure you feel valued, supported, and thrive at work:
• Private Healthcare • Employee Assistance Program
• Enhanced Maternity and Paternity Leave • Workplace Nursery Scheme
• Cycle to Work Scheme • Hybrid/Flexible Working
• Team Gatherings and Connection Boost!
Oxford Economics is an equal opportunity employer that is committed to diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, colour, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, or any other protected characteristic as outlined by local government laws.

Roboyo&nbsp;AI&nbsp;is a category shaper in Applied AI and Agentic Automation.&nbsp;We help leading enterprises move from automation projects and AI experiments into governed, production-grade systems that execute real work across workflows, processes,&nbsp;products&nbsp;and services.&nbsp;
Our heritage is in scaled enterprise automation; our future is&nbsp;Applied AI and&nbsp;Agentic&nbsp;Automation: autonomous agents, AI engineering squads, process orchestration, data and knowledge foundations, and human-in-the-loop governance embedded deeply into how our clients&nbsp;operate.&nbsp;
We are not here to sell AI theatre. We are here to turn AI into&nbsp;working systems, measurable&nbsp;outcomes&nbsp;and repeatable transformation programs.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
ABOUT THE ROLE&nbsp;
We are looking for a Senior Automation Engineer to design, develop and deliver enterprise-scale automation solutions using UiPath, Automation Anywhere and Python. This is a genuinely hands-on, multi-platform role: you will actively build solutions in all three technologies, not simply oversee delivery.&nbsp;
You will own technical delivery from design and development through testing, deployment and optimisation, working with clients and distributed delivery teams. This is a UK-based remote position with occasional travel for client engagements, project workshops and team activities.&nbsp;
As an L3 engineer, you will tackle complex technical problems independently, contribute to code quality and engineering standards, and support less experienced colleagues without being expected to act as a dedicated people manager.&nbsp;
KEY RESPONSIBILITIES&nbsp;
• Design, develop, test and deploy robust automation solutions using UiPath, Automation Anywhere A360 and Python.&nbsp;
• Own technical delivery across the automation lifecycle, including solution design, documentation, release and post-deployment optimisation.&nbsp;
• Build integrations with REST APIs, databases and enterprise applications; create maintainable Python applications and components beyond basic scripting.&nbsp;
• Develop reusable components and frameworks, applying secure coding, exception handling, logging and operational monitoring practices.&nbsp;
• Diagnose and resolve complex automation failures, integration issues and performance bottlenecks in development and production.&nbsp;
• Apply engineering standards across Git, peer review, automated testing and CI/CD; contribute to reliable deployments.&nbsp;
• Collaborate with architects, technical leads, analysts and clients to translate business needs into practical technical solutions.&nbsp;
• Support effort estimation, technical documentation, knowledge sharing and mentoring for junior and mid-level engineers.&nbsp;
• Keep current with automation technologies and identify practical opportunities to improve delivery and client outcomes.&nbsp;
MUST-HAVE QUALIFICATIONS &amp; COMPETENCIES&nbsp;
• 4+ years of hands-on experience designing, developing and delivering RPA or intelligent automation solutions; this does not mean four years in each individual technology.&nbsp;
• Strong hands-on UiPath development experience, including Studio, Orchestrator and REFramework.&nbsp;
• Strong hands-on Automation Anywhere development experience, particularly Automation 360 (A360) and Control Room.&nbsp;
• Strong practical Python development capability beyond basic scripting, including maintainable code, applications, integrations or reusable components.&nbsp;
• Demonstrable experience actively developing solutions across UiPath, Automation Anywhere and Python.&nbsp;
• Experience owning solutions from technical design and development through testing, deployment and support.&nbsp;
• Solid software engineering foundations, including debugging, exception handling, reusable code and testing.&nbsp;
• Experience with REST APIs, SQL/databases, JSON, Git and enterprise-system integration.&nbsp;
• Ability to investigate complex problems, communicate clearly with technical and non-technical stakeholders, and work independently in distributed teams.&nbsp;
• Based in the UK and willing to travel occasionally for client engagements, project workshops and internal collaboration.&nbsp;
NICE-TO-HAVE QUALIFICATIONS &amp; COMPETENCIES&nbsp;
• UiPath Advanced RPA Developer or equivalent certification; Automation Anywhere Advanced or Master RPA Professional certification.&nbsp;
• Experience with Power Automate, Power Platform or other automation technologies.&nbsp;
• Experience integrating with SAP, Salesforce, Microsoft Dynamics or similar enterprise applications.&nbsp;
• Familiarity with Azure, AWS or Google Cloud and CI/CD tooling such as Azure DevOps or GitHub Actions.&nbsp;
• Experience with intelligent document processing, such as UiPath Document Understanding or Azure Document Intelligence.&nbsp;
• Exposure to generative AI, Agentic AI or AI-enabled automation use cases.&nbsp;
• Experience in consultancy, client-facing delivery or Agile teams.&nbsp;
IDEAL CANDIDATE PROFILE&nbsp;
You are a pragmatic, hands-on engineer who enjoys building reliable solutions and solving difficult problems. You can move confidently between UiPath, Automation Anywhere and Python, take ownership with limited supervision, work directly with clients, write clear and maintainable code, and share knowledge with colleagues. You value delivery quality and practical outcomes over technology for its own sake.&nbsp;
WHAT WE OFFER&nbsp;
• A UK-based remote role, with opportunities to collaborate with international delivery teams and clients.&nbsp;
• The opportunity to work across multiple leading automation platforms rather than being restricted to one technology.&nbsp;
• Exposure to emerging AI and Agentic Automation capabilities as our offering evolves.&nbsp;
• A collaborative specialist consultancy environment that values initiative, technical expertise and practical problem-solving.&nbsp;
• Opportunities to broaden your technical skills and contribute to the development of our automation practice.&nbsp;
We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.
Privacy Notice: By applying, you consent to the processing of your personal data for recruitment purposes in line with our Privacy Policy: https://roboyo.global/data-privacy/

Join TRG Screen: Building World-Class Teams. One Expert at a Time.
Are you ready to be part of a dynamic team at the forefront of subscription spend management innovation?
At TRG Screen, we're not just redefining how organizations manage their subscription expenses – we're shaping the future of the industry. With cutting-edge solutions and a commitment to excellence, we empower businesses around the globe to optimize their subscription investments and drive sustainable growth.
Join us in our mission to revolutionize subscription management and make a meaningful impact on the way businesses access and utilize critical information. At TRG Screen, your talent and ambition will find a home, where opportunities for growth and advancement abound.
About TRG Screen TRG Screen is the leading provider of market data and subscription management technology and automation solutions, tailored to the unique needs of financial institutions and legal firms. Our integrated suite of solutions includes market data and subscription spend management, usage management, compliance reporting, and comprehensive managed services, which hundreds of clients worldwide use to remove cumbersome and inaccurate manual processes and gain control over market data and subscription costs at scale. For more than 25 years, TRG Screen has enabled businesses who rely on market data to monitor and strategically manage spending and usage of data and information services, including market data, research, software licenses, consulting and other necessary corporate expenses. TRG Screen solutions give decisionmakers full transparency into subscription spend and usage, enabling them to proactively manage subscription costs at scale, conduct more informed vendor negotiations, improve governance, and avoid unnecessary spending on these mission-critical business services. TRG Screen is headquartered in New York City, with offices in Europe and Asia, as well as a 24x7 client support center in Bangalore, India.
TRG Screen is a portfolio company of Vista Equity Partners, one of the world’s largest and most respected private equity firms.
Department: Human Resources&nbsp;
Reports to: CHRO&nbsp;
Location: Belfast, Northern Ireland &nbsp;
Level: Mid-level (5+ years of HR experience)&nbsp;
About the Role&nbsp;
We’re looking for a proactive, results-driven HR Manager who thrives in a fast-paced, dynamic environment and can effectively partner with business leaders and managers across the UK, continental Europe, and the US. In this role, you’ll provide HR support across these regions, managing the full employee lifecycle, including employee relations, talent management, workforce planning, and HR policies and practices. You’ll leverage modern HR systems, AI tools, and data-driven insights to drive efficiency, streamline processes, and enhance the employee experience. Working closely with the broader HR team, you’ll serve as a trusted advisor to employees and leaders, balancing strategic thinking with hands-on execution to support business objectives.&nbsp;
Key Responsibilities&nbsp;
HR Business Partnering &amp; Management Support&nbsp;
• Act as a strategic partner to business leaders, coaching managers on people matters such as performance, development, and team dynamics&nbsp;
• Translate business goals into practical people strategies and HR initiatives&nbsp;
• Use workforce data and insights to advise on headcount, engagement, retention, and organizational health&nbsp;
Global Talent Management&nbsp;
• Support talent processes across regions, including performance management, succession planning, and career development&nbsp;
• Partner with Talent Acquisition on hiring needs, onboarding, and internal mobility&nbsp;
• Help managers identify and develop high performers and build skills across teams&nbsp;
Employee Relations&nbsp;
• Serve as the first point of contact for employee concerns, handling investigations, disciplinary matters, grievances, and conflict resolution&nbsp;
• Provide clear, fair, and well-documented guidance to managers and employees&nbsp;
• Maintain compliant employee records and case documentation&nbsp;
Organizational Change &amp; Workforce Planning&nbsp;
• Support change initiatives such as restructures, role changes, and process improvements&nbsp;
• Contribute to workforce planning, forecasting, and succession needs&nbsp;
• Help managers and employees through transitions with clear communication and change-management support&nbsp;
HR Policy &amp; Employment Practices&nbsp;
• Develop, update, and communicate HR policies and employment practices that comply with employment law across relevant jurisdictions&nbsp;
• Advise on contracts, leave, compensation practices, and regulatory requirements&nbsp;
• Run HR audits and keep processes consistent and scalable&nbsp;
HR Systems &amp; AI Enablement&nbsp;
• Use ADP as the primary HRIS and payroll platform for employee data, reporting, and HR transactions, keeping data accurate and compliant&nbsp;
• Spot opportunities to improve HR processes with AI and automation, applying sound judgment on data privacy, bias, and responsible use&nbsp;
• Produce HR analytics and dashboards that give leadership actionable insight&nbsp;
Qualifications&nbsp;
Required&nbsp;
• 5+ years of progressive HR experience, ideally in a business partner, generalist, or HR manager role&nbsp;
• Hands-on experience with employee relations, including investigations and conflict resolution&nbsp;
• Working knowledge of employment law and HR best practices (and international or multi-jurisdiction exposure, ideally)&nbsp;
• Experience with an HRIS, ADP preferred&nbsp;
• Strong communication, coaching, and influencing skills, with the confidence to advise senior leaders&nbsp;
• Sound judgment, discretion, and a high standard of confidentiality&nbsp;
• Comfort with HR data and metrics, and an interest in applying AI tools to HR work&nbsp;
Preferred&nbsp;
• Experience supporting global or multi-region teams&nbsp;
• Experience in change management or organizational design&nbsp;
• CIPD, SHRM-CP/SCP, PHR/SPHR, or equivalent certification&nbsp;
• Bachelor’s degree in HR, Business, or a related field&nbsp;
What Success Looks Like&nbsp;
• Managers see HR as a trusted, responsive partner&nbsp;
• Employee relations issues are resolved fairly, quickly, and with strong documentation&nbsp;
• HR policies are current, compliant, and easy to follow&nbsp;
• HR processes are measurably faster or better thanks to AI and automation
Join TRG Screen and unlock your potential in an environment where innovation thrives, opportunities abound, and your contributions make a difference. We are an equal opportunities employer. We recognise and value the power of diversity in our workplace and are committed to being an employer of choice for everyone. We welcome and encourage applicants from all backgrounds. All applications for employment are considered strictly on the basis of merit.
At TRG Screen, we understand that diverse and inclusive teams are not just beneficial, they are essential to our success. We recognize that embracing diverse perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences fosters innovation, enhances problem-solving capabilities, and drives better business outcomes. By cultivating a culture of inclusion where every voice is heard and valued, we empower our world class teams to thrive, excel, and drive positive change.
We are proud of our diverse workforce and are dedicated to creating a safe and welcoming environment for all employees. People from various ethnicities, ages, genders, and abilities are encouraged to apply.&nbsp;
